--
checks/reviews/19-the-first-hire/grok.json-42-    "evidence": "Chapter 1’s case is fixed capacity (distribution centres) committed before any hire. Chapter 20 is on the calendar specifically to own ending employment, notice and severance (CONTEXT.md §5b, §6). BW7 and ordinary Dutch practice include proeftijd, during which either party may terminate with immediate effect. The same overclaim is in the decision strip: “the first employee converts a cost you could stop into one you cannot.” That irreversibility is jurisdiction-shaped and belongs in the ground box or in chapter 20, not in the portable argument.",
checks/reviews/19-the-first-hire/grok.json-43-    "fix": "“The first employee is usually the first cost that is expensive to stop: it falls due in the bad months as well as the good, and it cannot be cancelled on the same terms as a contractor’s invoice.” Point at chapter 20 for how it actually ends."
checks/reviews/19-the-first-hire/grok.json-44-  },
checks/reviews/19-the-first-hire/grok.json-45-  {
