checks/reviews/19-the-first-hire/codex.err-1558-**What this chapter would use it for.** The post narrates Gymdesk's 2020–2022 stretch in order:
checks/reviews/19-the-first-hire/codex.err:1559:COVID-driven churn survived, a decision after "a few failed experiments engaging 'growth' and
checks/reviews/19-the-first-hire/codex.err-1560-advertising agencies" that outside consultants would never understand the audience the way Galperin
checks/reviews/19-the-first-hire/codex.err-1561-did, and then two concrete first hires — a content-marketing/editor role in **June 2021** (a former
checks/reviews/19-the-first-hire/codex.err-1562-freelance writer with an SEO background, to double down on organic acquisition), followed later that
checks/reviews/19-the-first-hire/codex.err-1563-year by the first full-time customer-service hire, after customer service handled through Upwork
checks/reviews/19-the-first-hire/codex.err-1564-contractors "just wasn't working out." Galperin frames the June 2021 hire explicitly as a threshold
checks/reviews/19-the-first-hire/codex.err-1565-decision, not a scaling detail: *"This was a big decision for me personally — it's different engaging
checks/reviews/19-the-first-hire/codex.err-1566-freelancers for fixed term / cost work, than bringing on someone as a full time employee that you're
checks/reviews/19-the-first-hire/codex.err-1567-now responsible to make sure they are paid every month. It was here that we started to make the
checks/reviews/19-the-first-hire/codex.err-1568-transition from a one-man, owner run business to an actual company."* That sentence is the chapter's
checks/reviews/19-the-first-hire/codex.err-1569-thesis material, stated by the founder himself rather than authored by this book. The post also gives
checks/reviews/19-the-first-hire/codex.err:1570:a later checkpoint — 8 employees and 4 contractors by the end of 2022 — which lets the chapter show
checks/reviews/19-the-first-hire/codex.err-1571-that the employee/contractor line was a decision made repeatedly, not settled once.
