checks/reviews/19-the-first-hire/codex.err:1878:checks/sources.tsv:63:galperin-2023-covid	https://erangalperin.com/2023/05/12/building-a-fitness-tech-company-during-covid/	Eran Galperin — "Building A Fitness Tech Company During COVID", published 2023-05-12 (dateModified 2023-10-02), consulted 2026-08-06. Founder's own contemporaneous-retrospective account: the first full-time hire (content marketing/editor, June 2021) made after outside agencies failed, a second first-time hire for customer service after Upwork contractors were not working out, the framing of that decision as the shift from a one-man business to a company, and the end-2022 headcount split of 8 employees and 4 contractors. Founder's own account: weaker evidence class per §5, attributed as such in the prose. This is the "From business to company" predecessor the ch. 18 entry (§6i) named as linked in-text and left unfetched; the live page's title is "Building A Fitness Tech Company During COVID", not the linked anchor text.
checks/reviews/19-the-first-hire/codex.err-1879-checks/sources.tsv:84:rijks-schijnzelfstandigheid-2026	https://www.rijksoverheid.nl/themas/werk/zelfstandigen-zonder-personeel-zzp/aanpak-schijnzelfstandigheid	Rijksoverheid — "Aanpak schijnzelfstandigheid" (Ministerie van SZW), consulted 2026-08-28. Government page stating that the Belastingdienst has enforced fully against schijnzelfstandigheid again since 2025-01-01, the charges an employer pays after the fact (loonbelasting, premies werknemersverzekeringen, bijdragen Zvw, sometimes pension), and that client and zzp'er share responsibility for the correct contract. Closes the §6i ch. 19 enforcement gap; used in the ground box alongside BW7 art. 610/610a.
