checks/sources.tsv-57-pb-7	https://blog.pinboard.in/2016/07/pinboard_turns_seven/	Pinboard Blog — "Pinboard Turns Seven", 8 July 2016, consulted 2026-08-02. The year revenue was added to the published table: 2010-2016 revenue and funding rows, running costs of about $17K a year, and his stated reason for publishing (to encourage one- or zero-person businesses). Also supplies the annual-subscription confounder for the 2015 dip and 2016 rise.
checks/sources.tsv-58-pb-8	https://blog.pinboard.in/2017/07/eight_years_of_victory/	Pinboard Blog — "Eight Years of Victory", 9 July 2017, consulted 2026-08-02. Revenue through 2017 ($259K, the peak) and active users at 29K, alongside his own account of a year of travel in which support email went unanswered for weeks and a "reverse sabbatical" to stabilise the site.
checks/sources.tsv-59-pb-11	https://blog.pinboard.in/2020/07/pinboard_is_eleven/	Pinboard Blog — "Pinboard is Eleven", 9 July 2020, consulted 2026-08-02. The eleven-year table: revenue 2010-2020 ending at $212K, active users at 19K, and funding at zero in every year. The single source that carries both halves of ch. 16 — enough reached, and enough left undefended.
